# §13d G2–G4 statement gate: campaign-lint baseline on the base tree

`scripts/campaign_style_lint.py` (as <OUT>/scripts/lint.py) over `TCSlib/Complexity` of <OUT>/base
(the tip's tree, before this gate). Its FAIL lines naming the `TuringMachine` facade:
```
FAIL TCSlib/Complexity/TuringMachine.lean facade does not import child module `TCSlib.Complexity.TuringMachine.Build.Contract.Basic`
FAIL TCSlib/Complexity/TuringMachine.lean facade does not import child module `TCSlib.Complexity.TuringMachine.Build.Contract.Catalog`
FAIL TCSlib/Complexity/TuringMachine.lean facade does not import child module `TCSlib.Complexity.TuringMachine.Build.Contract.Embed`
FAIL TCSlib/Complexity/TuringMachine.lean facade does not import child module `TCSlib.Complexity.TuringMachine.Build.Contract.Lift`
FAIL TCSlib/Complexity/TuringMachine.lean facade does not import child module `TCSlib.Complexity.TuringMachine.Build.Contract.Seam`
FAIL TCSlib/Complexity/TuringMachine.lean facade does not import child module `TCSlib.Complexity.TuringMachine.Build.EmitIterBody`
FAIL TCSlib/Complexity/TuringMachine.lean facade does not import child module `TCSlib.Complexity.TuringMachine.Build.EmitIterEmbed`
style_lint: 24 FAIL, 32 WARN over 387 files
```
The rule looks for an intermediate facade at `<dir>/<dir>.lean` (`check_facade`: `child.parent /
(child.parent.name + ".lean")`), so every child of `Build/Contract/` already fails it at the base; the one
FAIL in elaboration.log §5 (`Build.Contract.Catalog`) is one of these, not new.
